    "narrative": "The Austin Waves roster presents a balanced attack today, with **Gunnar Henderson** (74.86) and **Jacob Wilson** (71.63) leading the charge as our clear-cut top plays. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from the matchup against Peralta, where his aggressive baserunning is amplified by the pitcher's slow delivery, offering a rare boost in our priority category of stolen bases. Meanwhile, **Jacob Wilson** earns a massive 19% boost due to the favorable matchup against Bradford. The decision to prioritize **Jackson Merrill** (69.72) in the outfield is also validated by his strong 13% dynamic platoon edge, making him a high-efficiency start against Bibee despite the moderate opponent xERA.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Coby Mayo**, who landed just outside our active threshold with a 42.34 score. While **Coby Mayo** remains a high-upside asset, he was edged out by the superior platoon and order stability offered by **Dominic Smith** and **Miguel Vargas**. We are monitoring the risk profile of our outfield, as **Luis Robert Jr.** (49.97) faces a challenging platoon disadvantage (-15%), and **Kyle Tucker** (51.57) and **Andy Pages** (46.78) are both contending with the elite arm of Henderson (2.84 xERA). While we are currently starting them for their pedigree, these spots remain the most volatile if the game environment shifts.\n\nManagers should remain alert for any late lineup shifts affecting **Drake Baldwin** or **Sam Antonacci**, who are serving as our table-setters in the lead-off spots. The current projections are heavily influenced by their favorable lineup positions, and any drop in order would necessitate an immediate re-evaluation of their daily efficiency scores. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** still sidelined and **Nasim Nunez** unavailable, we are relying on the depth of the middle infield to sustain our Roto production while navigating these tough matchups against the likes of Cease and Henderson.",
